      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here are five gritty archetypes for your street-level crime pieces: The **Silent Watcher**, a retired cop who now guards a corner peddling informant intel for dark coin; **The Market Flainer**, a low-slung drug dealer who relies on a shaky network of small-time hustlers rather than big-dog corporate buyers; and the **Broken Installer**, who uses his social engineering skills to fix connections in high-visibility locations, something he often can't get done for legitimate work. Then there's **Nick the Fence**, a quiet character who only interacts with the \"start\" of something before ignoring the \"fin,\" and **Willie**, a violent enforcer who avoids formal careers, preferring to work off the books by drinking and fighting. Remember to ground their dialogue in dialect and avoid metaphors about things that don't exist in the gritty world.",
