      "content": "Here are five updated archetypes with specific demographics and physical details to ground your story in reality:  \n\n1. **The Silent Watcher** is a 50s Black ex-police officer from Harlem, with a weathered, scarred face and a faded badge tucked in his waistband, often seen smoking cigarettes on bars that have no sign. He moves with a stiff, military gait, avoiding eye contact with anyone who doesn't know him.  \n\n2. **The Market Flainer** is a Latino street vendor from East Jersey, with spiky-dyed hair and worn-out sneakers, selling cheap snacks while operating a small, hidden alley. He operates with nervous energy, constantly scanning corners for threats and showing a familiarity with local gang marks.  \n\n3. **The Broken Installer** is an immigrant from Eastern Europe, around 35, with thick layers of dirt under his nails and a permanently tired look in his eyes. He often wears work boots that are too big for his feet, hiding a history of espionage in the political underground and using that to manipulate high-profile deals.  \n\n4. **Nick the Fence** is a middle-aged white man from a rural Midwest town, with a clean-cut but shifty appearance, always",
